Vendored from https://github.com/vinceliuice/Orchis-kde at commit
b2a96919eee40264e79db402b915f926436100ad (2025-10-18), plasma/desktoptheme/Orchis-dark.

Local change: scripts/recolor-orchis.py repaints the surface fills of panel,
popup and widget backgrounds with ArtixDarkRounded's Window background
(#05070a) and of tooltips with its Tooltip background (#0d1424), keeping
Orchis's opacity; shadows and blur masks are unchanged. The colours are
literal on purpose: in plasmashell, currentColor in the ColorScheme-Background
class resolved to light grey, so notifications and tooltips showed white text
on a pale card. Switch handles use the button text colour instead of the
button background so off switches stay visible on black. Re-run the script after re-vendoring or changing the scheme's
Window or Tooltip background:

    scripts/recolor-orchis.py kde/desktoptheme/Orchis-dark \
        --scheme kde/color-schemes/ArtixDarkRounded.colors --write
